# zhoda-mcp conventions

- Built on the Python `mcp` SDK (FastMCP). stdio transport by default,
  SSE optional via `ZHODA_CORE_URL`.
- Tools: `zhoda_clarify`, `zhoda_deliberate`, `zhoda_verdict`,
  `zhoda_transcript`, `zhoda_reputation`. Names and signatures must match
  docs/02-mcp-server.md.
- Tools return structured JSON, never prose walls — the host agent decides
  how to render.
- `zhoda_deliberate` must first return a cost/time estimate and require
  explicit confirmation from the host before running the full cycle.
- Long deliberations stream progress via MCP notifications so hosts
  don't kill the call on timeout.
- The core is embedded in-process by default; `ZHODA_CORE_URL` switches
  to a remote core over HTTP. No deliberation logic in this layer.
